<h2 id="by-wcag-h">Findings by WCAG success criterion</h2>
<p class="muted">A finding mapped to two criteria is listed under both. The criterion mapping is a static crosswalk and needs expert review before it is used as evidence.</p>
<section><h3>WCAG 1.1.1 Non-text Content (A); EN 301 549 9.1.1.1 (1)</h3><ul><li><a href="#fix-3">image-alt</a> — 1 occurrence on 1 page</li></ul></section>
<section><h3>WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (A); EN 301 549 9.1.3.1 (1)</h3><ul><li><a href="#fix-4">label</a> — 1 occurrence on 1 page</li></ul></section>
<section><h3>WCAG 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum) (AA); EN 301 549 9.1.4.3 (6)</h3><ul><li><a href="#fix-1">color-contrast</a> — 6 occurrences on 3 pages</li></ul></section>
<section><h3>WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A); EN 301 549 9.4.1.2 (1)</h3><ul><li><a href="#fix-4">label</a> — 1 occurrence on 1 page</li></ul></section>
<section><h3>Best practice (no WCAG success criterion mapped) (3)</h3><ul><li><a href="#fix-2">region</a> — 3 occurrences on 3 pages</li></ul></section>
</section>"
`;

exports[`HTML report v2 sections (snapshots) > section #how-to-fix 1`] = `
"<section id="how-to-fix" aria-labelledby="how-to-fix-h">
<h2 id="how-to-fix-h">How to fix, by rule</h2>
<p class="muted">A11yGate does not write alternative text, labels or accessible names. Any such text is a TODO for a person who knows the content, followed by human review.</p>
<section id="fix-1"><h3>color-contrast <span class="impact serious">serious</span></h3>
<p>Elements must meet minimum color contrast ratio thresholds</p>
<p><strong>Who is affected:</strong> People with low vision or color-vision differences may not be able to read the affected content.</p>
<p><strong>How to fix:</strong> Adjust foreground/background colors to meet the applicable contrast ratio; include hover, focus and disabled states where relevant.</p>
<p><strong>How to verify:</strong></p><ul><li>Re-run axe on the same page/state and affected selector.</li><li>Measure rendered contrast (normally 4.5:1 text or 3:1 large text); review gradients and dynamic states manually.</li></ul>
<p><strong>References:</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/color-contrast">Engine rule help<span class="sr"> for color-contrast</span></a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/contrast-minimum.html">W3C Understanding 1.4.3 Contrast (Minimum) (AA)</a></li></ul>
<p class="muted">Rule-based guidance; contextual human review required, not legal advice or certification.</p></section>
<section id="fix-2"><h3>region <span class="impact moderate">moderate</span></h3>
<p>All page content should be contained by landmarks</p>
<p><strong>Who is affected:</strong> The affected element may prevent people using assistive technology from perceiving or operating the content (region); assess the actual user journey.</p>
<p><strong>How to fix:</strong> All page content should be contained by landmarks Consult the rule guidance and review the actual component; automated advice is not a verified fix.</p>
<p><strong>How to verify:</strong></p><ul><li>Inspect the affected element and applicable rule guidance.</li><li>Re-run the same rule on the same page/state and manually verify the relevant keyboard/screen-reader journey.</li></ul>
<p><strong>References:</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/region">Engine rule help<span class="sr"> for region</span></a></li></ul>
<p class="muted">Rule-based guidance; contextual human review required, not legal advice or certification.</p></section>
<section id="fix-3"><h3>image-alt <span class="impact critical">critical</span></h3>
<p>Images must have alternative text</p>
<p><strong>Who is affected:</strong> People using screen readers may miss the purpose or information conveyed by the image.</p>
<p><strong>How to fix:</strong> Provide contextual alternative text for informative images; use empty alt for genuinely decorative images.</p>
<p><strong>How to verify:</strong></p><ul><li>Re-run axe on the same page/state and selector.</li><li>Listen with a screen reader and confirm the alternative conveys the same purpose without redundant detail.</li></ul>
<p><strong>References:</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/image-alt">Engine rule help<span class="sr"> for image-alt</span></a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/non-text-content.html">W3C Understanding 1.1.1 Non-text Content (A)</a></li></ul>
<p class="muted">Rule-based guidance; contextual human review required, not legal advice or certification.</p></section>
<section id="fix-4"><h3>label <span class="impact critical">critical</span></h3>
<p>Form elements must have labels</p>
<p><strong>Who is affected:</strong> People using assistive technology may not know what input is expected.</p>
<p><strong>How to fix:</strong> Associate a visible label with the control and expose instructions/errors programmatically.</p>
<p><strong>How to verify:</strong></p><ul><li>Inspect the accessible name and label association; re-run axe.</li><li>Navigate and complete the field using keyboard and a screen reader, including validation errors.</li></ul>
<p><strong>References:</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://dequeuniversity.com/rules/axe/4.14/label">Engine rule help<span class="sr"> for label</span></a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/info-and-relationships.html">W3C Understanding 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (A)</a></li><li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/name-role-value.html">W3C Understanding 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A)</a></li></ul>
<p class="muted">Rule-based guidance; contextual human review required, not legal advice or certification.</p></section>
</section>"
`;

exports[`HTML report v2 sections (snapshots) > section #limits 1`] = `
"<section id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-h">
<h2 id="limits-h">What automated testing does not cover</h2>
<p>This report records what automated rules detected on the pages listed above. It does not assess:</p>
<ul><li>Most WCAG success criteria need human judgement. Automated rules detect only a subset of accessibility barriers, so an empty findings list is not evidence of conformance.</li><li>Whether text alternatives, form labels, headings, link text and page titles are accurate and meaningful. Tools can only check that they exist.</li><li>Keyboard operability across complete user journeys, logical focus order, visible focus in context and keyboard traps that appear after interaction.</li><li>The experience with screen readers, magnifiers, voice control and other assistive technology.</li><li>Login journeys, forms, multi-step flows, error states, menus, dialogs and other interactions beyond the pages explicitly scanned.</li><li>Pages that were not reached: not linked through same-origin a[href] links, beyond the crawl cap, disallowed by robots.txt, or failed to load.</li><li>Captions, transcripts and audio description for time-based media, and whether they are correct.</li><li>Cognitive and learning accessibility: plain language, consistent navigation, timing, and error prevention and recovery.</li><li>Reflow, zoom, orientation and user style or contrast settings beyond what individual rules check.</li><li>Documents (PDF, office files), native apps, emails and third-party services that were not rendered in the scanned pages.</li></ul>
<p>Manual testing by people, including people with disabilities and assistive technology users, is needed for these areas.</p>
<h3>Scope and boundaries of this scan</h3>
<ul><li>Only scan sites you own or are explicitly authorized to test.</li><li>Automated testing only: axe-core detects a subset of WCAG issues. Absence of findings is not conformance, certification or legal advice.</li><li>Read-only: pages were loaded without logging in, filling forms or clicking. Authenticated areas, interactions and dynamic states are unassessed.</li><li>Only same-origin pages reachable through a[href] links (at most 20) were visited; robots.txt Disallow rules were honoured.</li></ul>
<h3>Not scanned</h3><ul><li><code>https://site.test/private/</code> — disallowed by robots.txt</li></ul>
</section>"
`;

exports[`HTML report v2 sections (snapshots) > section #shared-components 1`] = `
"<section id="shared-components" aria-labelledby="shared-components-h">
<h2 id="shared-components-h">Likely shared components</h2>
<p>Likely shared components are heuristic suggestions based on matching rules, normalized selector paths and similar HTML. Review examples to confirm whether one component fix applies. Finding totals and gate decisions are unchanged.</p>
<section><h3>color-contrast — likely shared component on 3 pages</h3><p>3 findings; normalized selector: <code>a.nav</code></p><ul><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/</code><br>Selector: <code>a.nav</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;a.nav&gt;</code></li><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/about</code><br>Selector: <code>a.nav</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;a.nav&gt;</code></li><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/contact</code><br>Selector: <code>a.nav</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;a.nav&gt;</code></li></ul></section><section><h3>color-contrast — likely shared component on 3 pages</h3><p>3 findings; normalized selector: <code>p.faint</code></p><ul><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/</code><br>Selector: <code>p.faint</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;p.faint&gt;</code></li><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/about</code><br>Selector: <code>p.faint</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;p.faint&gt;</code></li><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/contact</code><br>Selector: <code>p.faint</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;p.faint&gt;</code></li></ul></section><section><h3>region — likely shared component on 3 pages</h3><p>3 findings; normalized selector: <code>div</code></p><ul><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/</code><br>Selector: <code>div</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;div&gt;</code></li><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/about</code><br>Selector: <code>div</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;div&gt;</code></li><li>Example page: <code>https://site.test/contact</code><br>Selector: <code>div</code><br>HTML: <code>&lt;div&gt;</code></li></ul></section>
</section>"
`;

